                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 68-year-old male, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, he exhibited marked dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. Clinical response was satisfactory, with clear improvement in respiratory function and oxygen saturation. He is discharged in stable condition with a prescription for oral steroids taper and optimised inhaler therapy. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks and consider referral to pulmonary rehabilitation. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
